    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **35 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the codebase's existing duplicate-telephone pattern.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending lower-cased email, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` call in `addOwner` right after `normalizeEmail(...)` (so the submitted email is already trimmed/lower-cased), plus the helper method. It skips a `null` email (the field is optional) and otherwise compares the submitted email against every existing owner's email, lower-cased with the same locale, throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a match.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` returning `409 CONFLICT` with an `errors: [\"email\"]` property, consistent with the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe check is placed on the create path only (`addOwner`), matching the existing telephone/household duplicate checks, which are likewise create-only.",
